message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Complexity and Noise-Resilience of Quantum Oracles for Symmetric Cryptanalysis"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible study of Grover-based known-plaintext key search against a toy
  4-bit substitution-permutation network, executed under simulated NISQ noise,
  with classical readout-error mitigation. Includes exhaustive verification of
  the reversible encryption circuit against a classical reference.
